    "field": "Long-term variations of solar irradiance",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the challenge of characterizing long-term variations in surface solar radiation, countering the historical assumption of its stability by analyzing observational data that reveal widespread, multi-decadal trends of \"global dimming\" and subsequent \"brightening\" that are not fully understood.",
    "method": "This paper examines the long-term variation of global solar radiation by compiling and analyzing quality-controlled pyranometer measurements from a global network of approximately 400 observation sites, with a primary focus on the last 50 years.",
    "task": "The task is to examine long-term variations of global solar radiation at the Earth's surface by analyzing pyranometer measurements from approximately 400 sites to identify historical trends of dimming and brightening over the last 50 to 80 years.",
